e exit, sweeping across the black room, and settles at 30° on the BLACK INTERIOR DOORWAY in the far north-east corner. It is empty. Behind the camera, running feet arrive on gravel; two truck doors open and slam. 0:04–0:09 — The camera begins reversing toward the front door. Deep in the house, FOOTSTEPS: fast, then stopping dead. A pause. Then again, further off. Then closer. Behind the camera, overlapping and panicked: "Go — go, go—" / "I'm going, I'm going—" / "My phone's dead — it's like something drained it—" 0:09–0:12 — The camera passes out through the front door onto the porch, still backing away, framing NESTED DOORWAYS: the exterior doorframe holding the dark room, and small and deep within it, the black interior doorway. The footsteps stop. Silence. Behind camera: keys hit gravel — "Shit — I dropped 'em—" / "Danny!" 0:12–0:15 — Far away inside the house, a FIGURE begins easing out of that interior doorway — slowly and continuously, a sliver at a time: a shoulder, then an arm, then the brim of a cap, a pale smudge of face with two dark pits where the eyes should be. He is tiny in frame, deep in the black, and he never stops creeping fractionally further out. The camera keeps retreating down the steps. End frame: two nested doorways with something half-emerged in the far one. PHYSICS: Real weight in every offscreen sound — footsteps flexing real floorboards, keys bouncing on gravel. The figure's emergence is smooth, slow and continuous with no jerk and no pause. Corn moves in the wind. Air is dead still otherwise. LIGHTING: Dead midnight. Thin cold moonlight only — deep crushed blue-black with barely preserved shadow detail, no fill, no rim, no invented light, no practical lights anywhere. A single narrow shaft of moonlight from the front door reaches partway into the room and dies before the far doorway, so the figure is lit only at the very edge of it. AUDIO: Absolute country stillness — crickets, faint wind in the corn, air quiet enough that every sound carries. Footsteps inside the house: fast, stopping dead, further, closer, stopping again — irregular and unpredictable. The figure makes NO vocal sound of any kind. Behind the camera: running feet on gravel, two doors slamming, and overlapping panicked voices — "Go — go, go—" / "I'm going, I'm going—" / "My phone's dead — it's like something drained it—" / keys hitting gravel / "Shit — I dropped 'em—" / "Danny!". No music. No subtitles. CHARACTER ACTING: The figure is always distant and always partially hidden. His emergence is slow, smooth and continuous — never a pose, never static, always creeping a fraction further out of the black. No rage, no snarl, no sound; the wrongness is in how unhurried he is. He does not step into the room. STYLE Style: photorealistic 35mm film. No 3D render, no game engine, no game-cutscene aesthetic. Cinematography: composed, patient frames — locked or slow deliberate moves; painterly widescreen composition; strong silhouettes against practical light. Lighting: one-source logic, motivated practicals only — string lights, dash glow, streetlight, dome light, kitchen fixture; camera on the shadow side; low key throughout; no beauty fill, no studio light. Color: 60% blue-black night, 30% moonless deep blue, 10% warm amber practical light. Camera: physical cine lens, 180° shutter motion blur, fine organic film grain. Skin: pore-level realism, matte, vellus hair, no retouch. Acting: micro-pauses before reactions, precise eye-lines, wet living eyes with catch-lights, visible breath and chest rise. Physics: gravity and inertia respected — mass has real weight, correct contact shadows, no floating props. Continuity: characters, props, environment identical across every cut. No identity drift. Technical: 24fps smooth motion, no jitter. Audio: environmental SFX only. No music. No subtitles. QUALITY Coherent single continuous take, consistent character identity, no morphing, no extra people, no repeated or looping action. POSITIVE CONSTRAINTS The